      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "In 3D asset rendering, environment textures are the basis for image-based lighting algorithms where surfaces can realistically reflect light from their surroundings.",
      "normalizedSource": "In 3D asset rendering, environment textures are the basis for image-based lighting algorithms where surfaces can realistically reflect light from their surroundings.",
      "sourceHash": "16a50e57d18be264fb9f207815d23e7154811f34c680432d41b3e0eb80594be5",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Environment textures are cube-map textures that depict the view in all directions from a specific point in a scene.",
      "contextAfter": "ARKit generates environment textures during an AR session using camera imagery, allowing SceneKit or a custom-rendering engine to provide realistic image-based lighting for virtual objects in your AR experience.",
      "documentTitle": "ARWorldTrackingConfiguration.EnvironmentTexturing",
      "framework": "ARKit",
      "ko": "3D 자산 렌더링에서 환경 텍스처는 주변 표면이 주변광을 자연스럽게 반사할 수 있도록 하는 이미지 기반 조명 알고리즘의 기반이 됩니다.",
